443		with answers consisting of pairs of polynomials
444		$(f_X, f_Z) \in \deg_{md}(\ell_X) \times \deg_{md}(\ell_Z)$, such that on
445		average over pairs $(\ell_X, x)$ and $(\ell_Z, z)$ independently sampled
446		from the line-point distribution
