463		$(f_X, f_Z) \in \deg_{md}(\ell_X) \times \deg_{md}(\ell_Z)$, the sandwich
464		operator
465		$T^{\ell_X,\ell_Z}_{f_X,f_Z}
466		= \hat{M}^{(\mathrm{Line},X),\ell_X}_{f_X}
467		\hat{M}^{(\mathrm{Line},Z),\ell_Z}_{f_Z}
468		\hat{M}^{(\mathrm{Line},X),\ell_X}_{f_X}$,
469		which forms a valid POVM; since the lines measurements come from a valid
470		strategy for the low-degree test, on an axis-parallel line $\ell_W$ the
471		outcome $f_W$ lies in $\deg_d(\ell_W)$, and this property is inherited by
472		$T$. As intermediate consistency relations, write
473		$\hat{Q}^{x,z}_{a,\bullet} = \sum_b \hat{Q}^{x,z}_{a,b}$ and
474		$\hat{Q}^{x,z}_{\bullet,b} = \sum_a \hat{Q}^{x,z}_{a,b}$ for the two
